  "protocol": "Same static diagnostic server binary, uncached greedy 4000/64 requests, ignore EOS, seed 42, BF16 KV. Stock/retain/retain/stock process order. Each timed process gets a 15/8 warmup and two uncached requests. Full logits captured in separate fresh processes. TTFT starts at the request and includes the adoption before the first response token. Decode TPS is 63 divided by time between first and last token arrivals. End-to-end response time includes both. Concurrent Metal jobs were checked before and during runs. The OS file cache was uncontrolled.",
  "mechanism": "At 18 GiB both modes enter wide prefill with 36 resident decode layers and exactly two rotating prefill weight banks. After the final layer finishes, the experiment drains the prefill graphs, joins the read worker and moves the existing charged buffers for block indices 38/39 to the context resident set. A scheduler reset invalidates stale graphs at promotion and before releasing both banks for the next prefill. The experiment performs zero new expert reads or copies during promotion. The same prefill reads and kernels are used in both cases.",
